            <ArticleTitle>Perioperative myocardial infarction secondary to dynamic circumflex coronary artery occlusion after mitral valve repair.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Few reported cases document injury to the circumflex coronary artery secondary to repair of the mitral valve annulus. This potentially life-threatening sequela must be considered during mitral valve repair. In an effort to increase awareness of this sequela, we present the case of a patient who experienced a perioperative myocardial infarction secondary to injury of the circumflex coronary artery after mitral valve repair.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
